[ar:aarav_kharade1234]
[ti:What's Special]
[al:Bringing the world back]

[00:01.40]What's special?
[00:03.48]The thing that shines?
[00:06.48]The thing that everybody sees?
[00:09.34]No.
[00:11.28]Listen again.
[00:13.60]What's special...
[00:18.02]is usually small enough
[00:21.50]to miss.
[00:27.47]A shoelace comes undone
[00:29.53]halfway down the road,
[00:31.90]you stop beneath a traffic light,
[00:34.65]laugh at your own feet.
[00:37.36]A little kid is chasing pigeons,
[00:39.12]one gets away,
[00:42.00]he doesn't look disappointed.
[00:44.41]He chases another.
[00:47.05]A woman on the bus
[00:47.88]is humming something wrong,
[00:49.49]she knows every word
[00:50.39]but she forgot the song.
[00:51.95]And nobody applauds.
[00:53.29]Nobody turns around.
[00:56.04]Nobody says:
[00:57.06]"Look at that."
[00:58.06]Tick—
[00:58.74]wait.
[00:59.38]Tick-tick—
[01:00.30]move.
[01:00.87]Tap—
[01:01.35]breathe.
[01:01.91]One step—
[01:02.49]two—
[01:03.14]then three.
[01:03.72]You thought the groove was here.
[01:06.46]Not yet.
[01:08.14]You thought the moment was gone.
[01:10.30]Not yet.
[01:13.81]What's special?
[01:15.33]Not the tallest.
[01:16.43]What's special?
[01:17.83]Not the loudest.
[01:19.06]What's special?
[01:20.56]Not the one on the screen.
[01:24.19]Then what is?
[01:26.67]The thing that happens
[01:28.43]when nobody's looking.
[01:34.20]That's special.
[01:35.93]A man saves half his sandwich
[01:38.13]for a dog he doesn't know.
[01:40.29]A girl draws a crooked sun
[01:42.33]on the back of an old receipt.
[01:44.85]Two friends argue for an hour
[01:46.66]over absolutely nothing,
[01:49.34]then one of them says,
[01:50.18]"Fine."
[01:51.40]And both of them start laughing.
[01:53.97]A father carries his sleeping child
[01:55.26]three floors upstairs.
[01:57.14]He could've woken him.
[01:58.48]He doesn't.
[01:59.54]Because sometimes love
[02:01.32]is simply carrying the weight.
[02:04.19]What if the beautiful things
[02:06.43]never learned to advertise?
[02:08.12]What if the miracle
[02:09.10]doesn't need a camera?
[02:10.80]What if the best part of your life
[02:12.80]is happening right now
[02:14.27]and you're waiting
[02:15.33]for something bigger?
[02:16.51]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[02:17.45]It's the laugh that escapes
[02:18.46]before you can stop it.
[02:20.98]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[02:22.44]It's the person who remembers
[02:23.80]the tiny thing you forgot.
[02:26.34]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[02:27.67]It's the rain arriving
[02:28.98]before you reach the door.
[02:31.97]It's the song you can't explain.
[02:33.87]It's the scar nobody sees.
[02:36.72]It's the hand that finds yours
[02:39.35]when there is nothing left to say.
[02:42.03]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[02:45.93]Maybe...
[02:47.76]you are.
[02:49.09]There's a blue cup.
[02:49.74]Don't ask me why.
[02:50.98]A blue cup sits on a yellow table
[02:52.83]in a room with a broken clock.
[02:54.96]Someone left a flower beside it.
[02:57.16]The flower is dying.
[02:58.51]The clock is stopped.
[02:59.57]The cup is chipped.
[03:00.78]And somehow...
[03:01.48]the whole thing is perfect.
[03:03.50]Why?
[03:05.95]Nobody knows.
[03:07.28]That's the point.
[03:08.35]What's special?
[03:10.01]A voice.
[03:10.58]A smell.
[03:12.04]A place.
[03:12.81]A mistake.
[03:13.64]A goodbye.
[03:14.44]A stupid joke.
[03:15.52]The first rain.
[03:16.94]The last train.
[03:18.32]Someone waiting.
[03:19.81]Someone coming home.
[03:27.63]Who's right?
[03:28.57]Everybody.
[03:32.25]Maybe special isn't rare.
[03:34.13]Maybe that's the trick.
[03:36.04]Maybe we've been searching for diamonds
[03:39.41]while stepping over flowers.
[03:42.33]Maybe we've been waiting
[03:44.64]for fireworks
[03:45.43]while somebody beside us
[03:46.76]is quietly
[03:47.89]burning bright.
[03:56.04]You don't have to become extraordinary.
[03:59.09]You just have to
[04:01.70]be here.
[04:06.25]I know a boy who talks to himself
[04:08.45]when nobody's around.
[04:10.79]I know a girl who dances
[04:13.58]while brushing her teeth.
[04:15.83]I know a man who cries
[04:17.54]during old cartoons.
[04:19.55]I know a woman who still keeps
[04:21.44]a birthday card from ten years ago.
[04:23.65]And I know somebody
[04:25.58]who thinks they're ordinary.
[04:27.75]They aren't.
[04:28.82]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[04:31.33]The impossible little pattern
[04:33.04]that could never happen twice.
[04:34.41]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[04:36.72]Your ridiculous laugh.
[04:38.12]Your terrible dancing.
[04:40.12]Your perfectly timed mistake.
[04:44.32]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[04:45.65]The way you say someone's name.
[04:47.56]The way you look at the sky.
[04:50.60]The way you keep going
[04:51.90]without knowing why.
[04:55.95]WHAT'S SPECIAL?
[04:57.31]Not perfection.
[05:00.38]Not fame.
[05:01.27]Not being remembered
[05:02.90]by everybody.
[05:05.53]Just this:
[05:08.87]You were here.
[05:09.90]And for one impossible second,
[05:13.93]the universe
[05:14.96]looked exactly like this.
[05:18.67]What's special?
[05:22.78]You know.
[05:24.24]What?
[05:24.94]You noticed.
[05:27.21]That's enough.